---
import Content from "@/layouts/Content.astro";

/**
 * ⚠️ This document describes the site as it actually behaves TODAY: no
 * accounts, no analytics, no advertising, no network calls carrying user data.
 * That is an unusually strong claim and it is only true while it stays true.
 *
 * If analytics, an ad network, embedded video, or any third-party script is
 * ever added, this page MUST be updated in the same pull request. Under COPPA a
 * persistent identifier — an ad cookie, a device id, an analytics client id —
 * counts as personal information collected from a child, and shipping one while
 * this page says otherwise turns a technical change into a false statement.
 *
 * It renders in Line world, which has no scenery on purpose. Every other page
 * here is a place; this one is a promise being read carefully, and dressing it
 * up as an adventure would be the wrong kind of charming.
 */
const title = "Privacy — School Skills";
const description =
  "School Skills collects nothing. No accounts, no analytics, no advertising, no tracking. Everything a child does stays in their own browser.";
const updated = "12 August 2026";
---

<Content title={title} description={description} world="line">
  <header class="hero wrap">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">
      <span class="hero__world">Privacy</span>
      Updated {updated}
    </p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">We don&rsquo;t collect anything</h1>
    <p class="hero__lead">
      That is the whole policy. The rest of this page explains how that can be
      true, and what it means for you.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="band band--tight wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. There are no accounts, no sign-up, no email addresses, no
        analytics, no advertising, and no third-party scripts of any kind. We do
        not know who you are, how many of you there are, or that you visited.
      </p>

      <h2>How that&rsquo;s possible</h2>
      <p>
        School Skills is a static website. Every page is a file, served as-is
        &mdash; there is no application server, no database, and nothing for
        your child&rsquo;s answers to be sent to. When they finish a race, the
        result is written to your own browser&rsquo;s storage on your own
        device. It does not leave it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every file a page loads comes from this site, including the fonts. A
        font served from a font network would mean a request carrying your
        child&rsquo;s IP address to a third party on every page load, which
        would make the paragraph above untrue.
      </p>

      <h2>What&rsquo;s stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Player profiles (a name you choose, an emoji, a colour and an age), and
        the history of races played: times, scores, and which facts were
        answered right or wrong. This is kept in your browser&rsquo;s IndexedDB
        storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        You control it completely. Clearing your browser&rsquo;s site data
        deletes all of it permanently, and deleting a player in the app removes
        that player and every race they ran. Because we never receive any of it,
        we cannot restore it &mdash; which is why the app offers a backup file
        you keep yourself.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended for children and the adults helping them. We do
        not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, of any age,
        because we do not collect personal information at all &mdash; including
        the persistent identifiers (advertising IDs, analytics IDs, tracking
        cookies) that children&rsquo;s privacy law treats as personal
        information.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name you type for a player is stored only in your browser. We
        suggest a first name or nickname; nothing checks it, and nothing
        transmits it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We don&rsquo;t set any. There is no consent banner because there is
        nothing to consent to.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served from Amazon CloudFront. Like any web host, its
        servers process the standard request information needed to deliver a
        page &mdash; your IP address, browser type and the file requested
        &mdash; in short-lived operational logs. We do not use this to identify
        or track anyone, and it is never combined with anything from the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        There are no ads on this site today. If that ever changes, this page
        will be updated before any advertising code is added, and the change
        will be dated here.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Last updated {updated}. Material changes will be reflected in that date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@schoolskills.app"
          >hello@schoolskills.app</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Content>
